      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the product of solutions of the equation $2{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x+2}-32\\cdot {5}^{x+2}=0?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{x+2}-32\\cdot {5}^{x+2} & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-32)\\cdot {5}^{x+2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-32=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{5}^{x+2}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $2{x}^{2}-32=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}^{2}-16) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+4)(x-4) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-4,4.$\n\n- The equation $2=0$ is not a possible solution because it's a false statement.\n\n- The equation ${5}^{x+2}=0$ has no solutions because ${5}^{x+2}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-4,4,$ and their product is $(-4)\\cdot 4=-16.$",
